  "notes": "The sung-chorus wing of the Gotti camp, and the research gives a rare causal statement rather than a description: the loops are **two or three chords (i–VI–VII) *because* the melody is sung and needs motion**. So this entry gets real harmonic movement where its CMG neighbours get a drone — three moving families, no `impliedByRiff`, 32% sevenths and `topVoiceStepwise` on. The \"raised-6th / major-lift in the hook\" is authored as `dorian` sharing the scale weight with natural minor, which is exactly what a raised sixth in a minor key is. The 808 glides **following the sung melody's root motion**, so the glide lives with the bass rather than as an ornament (`bassline.glideProb` 0.32, `followRootsProb` 0.82 over a 20-semitone register). The mix note — **softer transients than the Youngsta / Big30 end of the CMG bench** — is why `velocityTiers` sit low and `snareRoll.rampJitter` is the smallest in the batch at 4, with the hat-roll frequency at the bottom of its band: restrained rolls, as described. The synth answering the vocal is a described part, so the countermelody runs at 0.55 above the lead with `fillGapsOnly` on, and the last hook doubling an octave up is why `octave_echo` carries real weight beside the answer lick. ⚠ `low`: the research rates it medium-low and says **the beat values are inferred** — `session.bpm` (66–78 half-time = 132–156 straight, marked [LOW-CONF]), the kick placement and the hat base are the inferred ones. The chart and certification, the label and the sung-hook role are what is sourced.",
